/-!
# A behaviour of THE target under H_RUNT(20 ps) that deadlocks, at g = 8/5, κ = 0 (shard C, 2026-11-07)

**Problem, plainly.** Under the owner's headline hypothesis H_RUNT(20) (a LUT input pin never reads inside a pulse
narrower than 20 ps), with no within-die scatter (κ = 0) but every
arc allowed anywhere in its fast-corner window widened by the guard g = 8/5, can THE target deadlock?

**Proved (if this file checks).** `xR` (generated by formal/tools/huff/simadv.py --classes --w 20 and
gen_runt_c.py) is a behaviour of `circuit DecodedPS.net DecodedPS.boundary` under `SpecRunt.BehavesRunt 20` at
`pK = ⟨8/5, 0⟩`, corner 0 (`behavesRunt_r`: every gate kernel-checked at every breakpoint; every LUT pin's read
map skips every pulse narrower than 20 ps, inside its delay window). Delays: the feedback pin (pin 0) of the
C-element ulink_n_falseResult_85 stage 0 (SLICE_X32Y45.A6) and the 6 pips/hops of its self-loop route at
⌊8·FAST_MAX/5⌋ (7 arcs, `slR`), every other arc at ⌈5·FAST_MIN/8⌉, LUT pins raised to at least 20 ps.
The C-element's acknowledge comes back before its own rise has gone round its slow feedback route; it oscillates
with pulses of 80-570 ps (which the runt filter does not touch) and the handshake is lost.

**Assumptions used.** Only Spec's and SpecRunt's definitions; standard axioms. The finite check `gateWR` and its
soundness are shard A's (CexRunt72/RBase), copied at g = 8/5, κ = 0 with per-arc slow lists.
-/

